---
import Main from '../../layouts/Main.astro';
---

<Main title='Carlos Gamez | About' bodyClass='about'>
  <main class='grid-container grid-container--about flow'>
    <p class='p-1'>I’ve always been drawn to making things.</p>

    <p class='p-2'>
      As a Design Engineer, I work across design systems, interaction design, and frontend development. I enjoy figuring out how an interface should look, how it should behave, and how to build it. That can mean shaping a component system, testing an idea through a prototype, or refining the details of a working product.
    </p>

    <p class='p-3'>
      Outside of work, I make music and build wooden furniture whenever I can. Both give me a different way to think about making: listening closely, working with constraints, and learning through small adjustments. I like seeing how individual decisions come together to shape the whole.
    </p>

    <p class='p-4'>
      I also spend a lot of time outside with my four huskies, two of them rescues. They bring plenty of chaos and give me a good reason to step away from the screen.
    </p>

    <p class='p-5'>
      Across all of these things, I’m drawn to the process of turning an idea into something you can use, hear, or hold.
    </p>
  </main>
</Main>

<style>
  .grid-container--about {
    --flow-space: 2rem;
    text-align: start;
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    grid-template-areas:
      'p1'
      'p2'
      'p3'
      'p4'
      'p5'
  ;

    & .p-1 {
      grid-area: p1;
    }

    & .p-2 {
      grid-area: p2;
    }

    & .p-3 {
      grid-area: p3;
    }

    & .p-4 {
      grid-area: p4;
    }

    & .p-5 {
      grid-area: p5;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 45em) {
    .grid-container--about {
      justify-items: start;
      align-content: start;
      grid-template-areas:
        '. p1 p1 .'
        '. p2 p2 .'
        '. p3 p3 .'
        '. p4 p4 .'
        '. p5 p5 .';
    }
  }
</style>
